  "description": "The 161 Poor Law Unions of Ireland after Donaghmore Union was dissolved on 30 Sep 1886, its divisions going to Abbeyleix and Roscrea, until Gortin was dissolved on 1 Apr 1889. Derived from the 5 Apr 1891 map with Gortin given back the divisions it held in 1851; divisions that moved between unions at dates not established between 1851 and 1891 are drawn as in 1891. Donaghmore's divisions are placed as the 1911 Queen's County table places them, the 1891 report not being held (workhouses.org.uk also names Urlingford, which has none of them by 1911). See Poor Law Unions 5 Apr 1891 for the method, the checks against the printed areas and the approximations (King's County, Queen's County, Carlow), all of which apply here. The map is simplified for display by a coverage simplification of the division map, so neighbouring unions keep common edges (95% of divisions lie within 10 m of the full lines); the full-resolution file is among the downloads.",
